Visibility annotations in a script. The exact form directly above
:PROCEDURE is effective (visibility_annotation_usage, info tier only).
Near-miss spellings, a detached annotation (blank line), one followed by a
:DECLARE, and one sharing a line are inert (diag.visibility_annotation,
warning). An annotation before an expression statement attaches to nothing
and gets neither code.
-- input.ssl --
/*@private;
:DECLARE nCount;
/*@private;
nCount := 1;

/*@private;
:PROCEDURE Effective;
	:RETURN 1;
:ENDPROC;

/*@Private;
:PROCEDURE NearMissCase;
	:RETURN 2;
:ENDPROC;

/* @protected;
:PROCEDURE NearMissSpace;
	:RETURN 3;
:ENDPROC;

/*@private;

:PROCEDURE Detached;
	:RETURN 4;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
/*@private;
:DECLARE nCount;

/*@private;
nCount := 1;

/*@private;
:PROCEDURE Effective;
	:RETURN 1;
:ENDPROC;

/*@Private;
:PROCEDURE NearMissCase;
	:RETURN 2;
:ENDPROC;

/* @protected;
:PROCEDURE NearMissSpace;
	:RETURN 3;
:ENDPROC;

/*@private;

:PROCEDURE Detached;
	:RETURN 4;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:12 warning visibility_annotation: Visibility annotation '/*@private;' should appear on its own line immediately before ':PROCEDURE'
11:1-11:12 warning visibility_annotation: '/*@Private;' is not a recognized visibility annotation, so the procedure stays public — write exactly '/*@private;' (lowercase, no spaces)
16:1-16:15 warning visibility_annotation: '/* @protected;' is not a recognized visibility annotation, so the procedure stays public — write exactly '/*@protected;' (lowercase, no spaces)
21:1-21:12 warning visibility_annotation: Visibility annotation '/*@private;' must sit on its own line immediately before ':PROCEDURE' — a blank line, another comment, or a shared line breaks the association, so the procedure stays public
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
